From 38b2411ef9138a5355a20272f2fe632a6c0903eb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: fozzfut <vanolia13@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 21:15:35 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] Main: finalise Python before exit() on the SystemExit path

sys.exit() (the -t test runner, the Python console, macros) leaves the event
loop through Base::SystemExitException, and main() then called exit() while
Python was still initialised. With PySide 6.11 / Python 3.14 the DLL static
destructors (shiboken's BindingManager, Qt's global QObjects) then tear down
wrappers of widgets that were already deleted: access violation in
shiboken6 during process exit, reported as "Abnormal program termination" /
"Break signal occurred" plus a crash report. The normal exit path finalises
Python in App::Application::destruct() and does not crash.

Finalise the interpreter before exit() on this path. Preferences are still not
saved on sys.exit(), as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/Main/MainGui.cpp | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/Main/MainGui.cpp b/src/Main/MainGui.cpp
index fba42a6..28af056 100644
--- a/src/Main/MainGui.cpp
+++ b/src/Main/MainGui.cpp
@@ -347,6 +347,13 @@ int main(int argc, char** argv)
         }
     }
     catch (const Base::SystemExitException& e) {
+        // sys.exit() (the -t test runner, the Python console, a macro) leaves the event loop
+        // through this exception. exit() alone would run the DLL static destructors while
+        // Python is still initialised: shiboken's binding manager and Qt's global objects
+        // then tear down wrappers of widgets that are already deleted, which aborts the
+        // process ("Abnormal program termination"). Finalise Python first, as the normal
+        // exit path does in App::Application::destruct().
+        Base::Interpreter().finalize();
         exit(e.getExitCode());
     }
     catch (const Base::Exception& e) {
-- 
